//? Title: Ukkonen suffix trees: actual phases and compressed edges
//? Subtitle: Actual native state, retained fixtures and explicit limits
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Repeated substring queries benefit from indexing all suffixes once. A compressed
suffix tree represents every substring as a prefix of a root-to-node path while
sharing repeated text.
)

\toc

> The method

Ukkonen maintains an active node, edge and length while appending each byte,
then a distinct virtual terminal256. Missing transitions add leaves; mismatching
edge interiors split an edge; matching interiors defer remaining suffix work.
Suffix links and skip/count hops amortize rescanning. Ordered maps give O(n log
σ) construction for bounded byte alphabet σ≤257, O(m log σ) lookup and O(n)
nodes. Sum actual edge lengths excluding one terminal per leaf to count distinct
nonempty substrings.

> Simple worked example

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/ukkonen_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r = a::build_suffix_tree_work("aba");
    std::print("| phase | actual nodes |\n|---:|---:|\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < r.nodes_after_phase.size(); ++i)
        std::print("|{}|{}|\n", i, r.nodes_after_phase[i]);
    std::print("\nActual splits {}; distinct substrings {}.\n", r.splits,
               a::distinct_substring_count(r.tree));
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Bytes aba and virtual terminal256");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("{} phases; {} splits", r.phases, r.splits));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("{} distinct substrings",
                                     a::distinct_substring_count(r.tree)));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/ukkonen_tiny.svg");
}
```
