> Interpretation and limits

Text and patterns are byte strings, including embedded NULs. The virtual
terminal is not a literal dollar byte; $ is merely its figure glyph. Tree
consumers assume an unmodified canonical tree. Diagram layout is iterative, so a
deep tree does not recurse. One million input bytes is the explicit construction
ceiling.

Every figure is saved locally by its complete editable program. No separate
reconstruction supplies algorithm state. Counters describe the selected events,
not elapsed time or peak memory.

> References

- [Ukkonen, On-line construction of suffix trees|https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01206331]

